---
const takes = ['Names', 'Circuit', 'Bad rows'];
const rows = [
  { y: 0, x: 0, valid: false }, { y: 0, x: 1, valid: true },
  { y: 1, x: 0, valid: true }, { y: 1, x: 1, valid: false },
];
---
<section class="perspectives" data-perspectives aria-labelledby="perspectives-title">
  <h2 id="perspectives-title">The same idea, three ways</h2>
  <p>Try a different starting point. Each view explains the same trick: give a piece a name, then make the name tell the truth.</p>
  <div class="take-buttons" data-take-controls hidden role="group" aria-label="Ways to explain Tseitin">
    {takes.map((take, index) => <button type="button" data-take={index} aria-pressed={index === 0}>{take}</button>)}
  </div>

  <section class="take" data-take-panel="0" aria-label="The naming explanation">
    <span class="take-number">01 / THINK LIKE A PROGRAMMER</span>
    <h3>A name is a promise</h3>
    <p>Imagine extracting a nested expression into variables. You haven’t changed the computation; you’ve given its intermediate results names.</p>
    <div class="program" aria-label="The formula as a small program">
      <div><span class="y1">y₁</span> := x₁ OR x₂</div>
      <div><span class="y2">y₂</span> := (<span class="y1">y₁</span> EQUALS x₃)</div>
      <div><span class="y3">y₃</span> := NOT x₄</div>
      <div><span class="y4">y₄</span> := (<span class="y2">y₂</span> IMPLIES <span class="y3">y₃</span>)</div>
      <div class="assert">require <span class="y4">y₄</span> = 1</div>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>What changes when a SAT solver reads this?</summary>
      <p>A program computes y₁ from its inputs. A solver can choose values for all the variables at once. So each assignment above becomes a constraint: <em>whatever values you choose, this equality must hold.</em> The CNF clauses enforce those promises.</p>
    </details>
    <p class="takeaway">The extra variables are intermediate results, not extra freedom.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="take" data-take-panel="1" aria-label="The circuit explanation">
    <span class="take-number">02 / FOLLOW THE WIRES</span>
    <h3>Give every gate an output wire</h3>
    <p>The formula is a small circuit. Each y names a wire leaving a gate. Flip an input and follow the values to the final output.</p>
    <div class="inputs" data-circuit-controls hidden role="group" aria-label="Circuit inputs">
      {[1, 2, 3, 4].map(id => <button type="button" data-circuit-input={id - 1} aria-pressed="false">x{['₁', '₂', '₃', '₄'][id - 1]} = <span>0</span></button>)}
    </div>
    <svg class="circuit" viewBox="0 0 520 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="circuit-title circuit-description">
      <title id="circuit-title">The four gates of the worked formula</title>
      <desc id="circuit-description">x₁ and x₂ feed OR to produce y₁. y₁ and x₃ feed EQUALS to produce y₂. x₄ feeds NOT to produce y₃. y₂ and y₃ feed IMPLIES to produce y₄.</desc>
      <g class="wires" fill="none">
        <path d="M45 40 H90 V60 H115 M45 100 H90 V80 H115" />
        <path d="M205 70 H242 V100 H270 M45 150 H242 V125 H270" />
        <path d="M45 235 H115" />
        <path d="M360 112 H400 V150 H420 M205 235 H400 V175 H420" />
      </g>
      <g class="input-labels"><text x="8" y="45">x₁</text><text x="8" y="105">x₂</text><text x="8" y="155">x₃</text><text x="8" y="240">x₄</text></g>
      <g class="gate y1"><rect x="115" y="43" width="90" height="54" rx="9" /><text x="160" y="77">OR</text><text class="wire-value" x="168" y="120" data-wire="0">y₁ = 0</text></g>
      <g class="gate y2"><rect x="270" y="86" width="90" height="54" rx="9" /><text x="315" y="120">EQUALS</text><text class="wire-value" x="315" y="163" data-wire="1">y₂ = 1</text></g>
      <g class="gate y3"><rect x="115" y="208" width="90" height="54" rx="9" /><text x="160" y="242">NOT</text><text class="wire-value" x="270" y="269" data-wire="2">y₃ = 1</text></g>
      <g class="gate y4"><rect x="420" y="137" width="92" height="54" rx="9" /><text x="466" y="171">IMPLIES</text><text class="wire-value" x="460" y="217" data-wire="3">y₄ = 1</text></g>
    </svg>
    <p class="circuit-readout" data-circuit-result aria-live="polite">Output y₄ = 1. The formula is true.</p>
    <p class="takeaway">Each gate gets a few clauses that enforce its behavior. Then require the final wire to be 1.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="take" data-take-panel="2" aria-label="The forbidden rows explanation">
    <span class="take-number">03 / RULE OUT THE LIES</span>
    <h3>A clause can ban a wrong answer</h3>
    <p>Zoom in on just the NOT gate: <span class="y3">y₃</span> must be the opposite of x₄. There are only four possible assignments. Two tell the truth; two lie.</p>
    <div class="truth-table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">y₃</th><th scope="col">x₄</th><th scope="col">Does y₃ = NOT x₄?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr><td>{row.y}</td><td>{row.x}</td><td>{row.valid ? '✓ yes' : '× no — forbid this row'}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="bad-row-buttons" data-row-controls hidden role="group" aria-label="Choose a forbidden row">
      <button type="button" data-bad-row="0" aria-pressed="true">Ban (0, 0)</button>
      <button type="button" data-bad-row="1" aria-pressed="false">Ban (1, 1)</button>
    </div>
    <div class="ban-explanation" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
      <p data-ban-formula><span class="y3">y₃</span> ∨ x₄</p>
      <p data-ban-description>This clause fails only at (0, 0): both literals are false. Requiring it to pass bans that row.</p>
    </div>
    <p>For (1, 1), use (¬<span class="y3">y₃</span> ∨ ¬x₄). AND both clauses together and only the two truthful rows survive.</p>
    <p class="takeaway">CNF is a collection of small rules that leave no room for the wrong gate outputs.</p>
  </section>
</section>

<style>
  .perspectives { --y1: #1769aa; --y2: #7b42ae; --y3: #a44814; --y4: #16735b; --line: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 18%, var(--bg)); margin-block: 2.5rem 3rem; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .perspectives { --y1: #83bcff; --y2: #cea2ff; --y3: #ffb47e; --y4: #7bdbb5; } }
  .y1 { color: var(--y1); } .y2 { color: var(--y2); } .y3 { color: var(--y3); } .y4 { color: var(--y4); }
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .take-buttons, .inputs, .bad-row-buttons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.45rem; }
  button { min-height: 44px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.5rem 0.85rem; font: 500 0.85rem/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); cursor: pointer; }
  button[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: var(--accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, var(--bg)); }
  button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .take-buttons { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .take { padding: 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .take-number { font: 600 0.68rem/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--ink); opacity: 0.65; }
  .perspectives .take h3 { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.9rem; font: 500 1.5rem/1.2 'Fraunces', serif; }
  .take p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .program { padding: 1rem; margin-block: 1.4rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 4%, var(--bg)); border-radius: 6px; font: 0.93rem/2 ui-monospace, monospace; overflow-x: auto; white-space: nowrap; }
  .assert { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 0.6rem; padding-top: 0.6rem; }
  details { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .perspectives .takeaway { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-weight: 500; }
  .inputs { margin-block: 1rem; }
  .inputs button { flex: 1; white-space: nowrap; padding-inline: 0.4rem; }
  .circuit { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin-block: 1rem; }
  .wires { stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; opacity: 0.5; }
  .circuit text { font: 600 14px system-ui, sans-serif; fill: currentColor; }
  .gate rect { fill: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 7%, var(--bg)); stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gate text { text-anchor: middle; font-size: 12px; }
  .gate .wire-value { font-size: 16px; }
  .circuit-readout { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .truth-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .perspectives table { width: 100%; font-size: 0.87rem; }
  .perspectives th, .perspectives td { padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .bad-row-buttons { margin-block: 1rem; }
  .ban-explanation { padding: 1rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 4%, var(--bg)); border-radius: 6px; }
  .perspectives [data-ban-formula] { font: 1.4rem/1.5 'KaTeX_Main', serif; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .perspectives [data-ban-description] { margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .take { padding: 0.9rem; } .program { font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.7rem; } .perspectives th, .perspectives td { padding: 0.45rem 0.25rem; } }
</style>

<script>
  import { deriveAuxiliaries } from '../lib/tseitin';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-perspectives]').forEach(root => {
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-take-controls], [data-circuit-controls], [data-row-controls]').forEach(controls => controls.hidden = false);
    const panels = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-take-panel]');
    function showTake(index: number) {
      panels.forEach(panel => panel.hidden = Number(panel.dataset.takePanel) !== index);
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-take]').forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(Number(button.dataset.take) === index)));
    }
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-take]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => showTake(Number(button.dataset.take))));
    showTake(0);
    const inputs = [false, false, false, false];
    const subscripts = ['₁', '₂', '₃', '₄'];
    function updateCircuit() {
      const outputs = deriveAuxiliaries(inputs);
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-circuit-input]').forEach(button => {
        const index = Number(button.dataset.circuitInput);
        button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(inputs[index]));
        button.querySelector('span')!.textContent = inputs[index] ? '1' : '0';
      });
      root.querySelectorAll<SVGTextElement>('[data-wire]').forEach(wire => {
        const index = Number(wire.dataset.wire);
        wire.textContent = `y${subscripts[index]} = ${Number(outputs[index])}`;
      });
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-circuit-result]')!.textContent = `Output y₄ = ${Number(outputs[3])}. The formula is ${outputs[3] ? 'true' : 'false'}.`;
    }
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-circuit-input]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const index = Number(button.dataset.circuitInput);
      inputs[index] = !inputs[index];
      updateCircuit();
    }));
    updateCircuit();
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-bad-row]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const bothTrue = button.dataset.badRow === '1';
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-bad-row]').forEach(other => other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === button)));
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ban-formula]')!.textContent = bothTrue ? '¬y₃ ∨ ¬x₄' : 'y₃ ∨ x₄';
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ban-description]')!.textContent = bothTrue
        ? 'At (1, 1), both negated literals are false. This clause fails only on that row, so requiring it to pass bans the other lie.'
        : 'This clause fails only at (0, 0): both literals are false. Requiring it to pass bans that row.';
    }));
  });
</script>
